# Namleh Agent Observability

Use this when agent work needs to become visible, auditable, and useful to
humans.

## Events To Capture

- workflow/skill invoked
- repo, branch, issue/PR, and project
- files changed
- tests and validations run
- security checks and findings
- deployment or CI result
- handoff created
- blocker or user decision required

## Avoid

- secrets, tokens, raw env values, cookies, PII
- hidden behavioral tracking
- noisy token/LOC vanity as the lead metric
- dashboards without actionability

## Useful Views

- current workstream status
- release readiness
- security review history
- QA evidence by workflow
- model benchmark history
- handoff queue for Tim
- failed/blocked automations

## Output

```text
Event Model:
- fields

Storage:
- local/repo/Ops Platform

Dashboard:
- views and filters

Privacy:
- redactions and access rules

First Implementation:
- smallest useful slice
```
